vron check list
- methods are decided deterministically
- each vron is capable of all methods (active and idle) (consilder goals as methods)
- each method has input and outputs
- method list
    - respond 
    - consildate (generate summary) 
    - query memory 
    - test 
    - react (same old mindstate scores)
    - plan
    - prompt user (proactive msg)
    - context swap.

-vron rules
- each vron is first created empty, ie make a queue of vron availablity
- each vron has a common max context (10k chars| 2,618 tokens) and is allowed to make a single api call (or two calls: an embedding call + llm call)
- the empty vron awaits use, and the max number of waiting vrons is decided by api limits, for now, we can have a max of 12/min (api itself allows upto 14/min)
- the empty queue is recharged affter every 60 seconds.
- each method costs energy, more context: more energy used
- api calls themselves do not cost energy, but they consume empty vrons

vron life cycle
- adding into the queue, as a new vron, empty and inactive, with an id, status: new
- a previous vron or determinsitic schedular uses the vron from the empty queue, assignign it a method and status: active|waiting|idle|terminated.
- the vron starts executing, the method may call other methods, a vron cannot create a new vron, it can only use what is available in the empty vron queue.
- the queue is refreshed every minute.

